128
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:30,840
It came from a new scout master who's been a scout master

129
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:31,840
for about a year,

130
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:34,840
Had a behavior problem at summer camp recently,

131
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:36,840
something pretty serious

132
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:39,840
And I'm not going to go into details about exactly what it was,

133
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:43,840
but had a similar problem with the same scout at a previous

134
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:45,840
camp and had a conference with the scout

135
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,840
And the parent thought it worked out. after the most recent

136
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:49,840
incident

137
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,840
They took the position that the scout should probably be

138
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:53,840
removed from the troop.

139
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:56,840
The parent defended the actions of the scout and claims that

140
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:59,840
the troop didn't do enough to prevent the incident.

141
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:02,840
So they had to feel through this situation here-

142
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:05,840
not a very good one, very difficult situation.

143
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:08,840
Ultimately they got the chartered organization involved

144
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:10,840
and the chartered organization's decision was to remove

145
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:11,840
the scout from a troop.

146
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:14,840
And this scouter wrote in to ask me if I agreed with

147
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:17,840
the decision or if I've heard of anything similar.

148
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:20,840
And indeed I have, and I'm sorry to hear about that

149
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:21,840
kind of trouble-

150
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:24,840
And I haven't had to deal with the particular behavior

151
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:26,840
described in this email,

152
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,840
But I've dealt with bad behavior that results in

153
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,840
removing a scout from the troop.

154
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:33,840
It's a pretty traumatic thing to do

155
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,840
And it's a pretty traumatic thing to go through as a

156
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:40,840
scouter, and anybody who has to do that has my sympathies.

157
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:43,840
Now, this is not something that happens all the time.

158
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,840
It's not a regular occurrence.

159
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:48,840
In my 30 plus years as a scouter I can only recall

160
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:51,840
one incident that was serious enough to merit

161
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,840
having to do this.

162
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:56,840
And you know, no matter how ardently we believe in our

163
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,840
scouts and how hard we try and help them,

164
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:00,840
sometimes it's just not going to work

165
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:04,840
And thankfully that is a rare situation,

166
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:07,840
But it can really knock the wind out of you as a scouter.

167
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:10,840
Now I won't second guess the decision that was made

168
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:12,840
or the way it was made.

169
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,840
It sounds like everything was handled well in this

170
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:15,840
situation

171
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:18,840
And this kind of decision is ultimately the charter

172
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:20,840
organization's decision in consultation with the

173
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,840
troop committee, who's also talking with the

174
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:25,840
scout master and assistant scout masters.

175
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,840
Then you also involve the scout executive in this

176
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,840
particular thing,

177
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,840
And that's sometimes an important part of arriving at

178
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:33,840
a workable resolution.

179
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:36,840
My guess is, if you're like me, there's at least a

180
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:38,840
shadow of doubt in your mind whether you did the

181
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:39,840
right thing or not.

182
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,840
I think that would be true of most of the people

183
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:43,840
listening, because the point of our volunteering is

184
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,840
because we really believe in young people,

185
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,840
And when we have to take a step like this,

186
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,840
it's very discouraging

187
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:51,840
And I think there's a lot of second guessing involved,

188
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:53,840
if you're like me, especially if a parent

189
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,840
accuses you of not having done enough to

190
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,840
prevent what happened.

191
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:00,840
Whenever I bring up a behavior problem with a

192
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:03,840
parent, usually they react by defending their

193
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:04,840
child.

194
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,840
I kind of expect it, because I think that's the

195
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,840
same way I would react if I was confronted with

196
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:10,840
a problem that my child caused.

197
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:13,840
But what's really most important is that

198
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,840
scouting happens in an atmosphere of mutual

199
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:18,840
trust and brotherhood rather than a matrix

200
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:20,840
of rules and regulations.

201
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:23,840
The rational measures we take to protect our

202
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:25,840
scouts from harm can't prevent

203
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,840
every possible problem.

204
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:29,840
I've been through a lot of difficult situations,

205
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:32,840
and some still cause me some discomfort

206
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,840
when I think about them and I wonder if I

207
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,840
could have handled them better,

208
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,840
But I've come to understand that that discomfort

209
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,840
is evidence of the sensitivity

210
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:43,840
required of anybody who's going to spend

211
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,840
their time working with young people.

212
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:47,840
After I sent that reply, the writer got back

213
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:49,840
to me and said: thanks for your words of

214
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:51,840
encouragement and advice.

215
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,840
Your reply helps me tremendously to deal

216
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:55,840
with the second thoughts in my head after

217
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:56,840
going through this.

218
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:58,840
The most difficult part was some people in

219
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:00,840
the troop wanted to offer a provisional

220
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:02,840
membership to the scout if their parent

221
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,840
attended or something like that, and I

222
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,840
disagreed and we're still working that

223
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:07,840
out.

224
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,840
Well, I've heard the idea of allowing a

225
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:11,840
scout to continue on who's been a

226
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,840
behavior problem if their parent is

227
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,840
going to be present all the time,

228
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,840
But it's not going to work because

229
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,840
scouting doesn't work that way.

230
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,840
There's no way to have authentic scouting,

231
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:23,840
with a parent who is going to be

232
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,840
there, closely involved in the

233
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,840
oversight of a scout's behavior.

234
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:29,840
That sort of arrangement would

235
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:31,840
fundamentally change the experience

236
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:33,840
for all the scouts involved and not

237
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:35,840
just this particular scout.

238
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:37,840
And while we're on the subject, there

239
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:39,840
are very few times when you're going

240
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,840
to be faced with the prospect of

241
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:43,840
having to remove somebody from a unit.

242
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:45,840
A pattern of serious misbehavior

243
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,840
is something that you have to deal with.

244
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:49,840
Take the scout, sit down with their

245
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:51,840
parents and say: you have to correct

246
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:53,840
this behavior, otherwise he can't be

247
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:55,840
a part of our troop. Sometimes that

248
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,840
will fix the problem, but sometimes the

249
00:11:57,840 --> 00:11:59,840
behavior goes on and then you have

250
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:01,840
to take the action that you took.

251
